# Keep the Docker build context small and reproducible.
target/
.git/
tests/donat/tests-py/
**/*.log
.claude/
# Installed dependencies and scratch apps. Neither is build input — `npm ci`
# recreates the first inside the image — and both are hundreds of megabytes
# that change constantly. Every change to them invalidates the layer that
# copies the tree, which turns an incremental image build into a full
# recompile of the Rust workspace. Measured, not assumed: editing a file under
# `experiments/` rebuilt the engine from scratch.
**/node_modules/
apps/ui/dist/
experiments/
# knowledgebase/ is NOT excluded: it is build input, not documentation.
# crates/connector-catalog/src/canonical.rs embeds ADR 012 with include_str!
# and parses the owner manifest out of it at compile time, so excluding the
# directory fails the build outright (and did — the image never published).
# 716K of markdown; keep it in the context until nothing `include_str!`s it.
